    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40530" root="نكر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْكَرُ</span></b>  <i>Worse,</i> and <i>worst; more,</i> and <i>most, evil,
abominable,</i> or <i>foul.</i> So it is explained as occurring in the Kur. [xxxi. 18,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنّ أَنْكَرَ ٱلْأَصْوَاتِ لَصَوْتُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَمِيرِ</span> [<i>Verily the most abominable of voices is
the voice of asses</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَكِرٌ</span>: and
the fem., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَكْرَآءُ</span>, see above.

